# Performance

- Keep client-side JavaScript minimal.
- Avoid unnecessary `useEffect`, `useState` and client fetching.
- Avoid duplicate API/database requests.
- Use optimized images and `next/image` where appropriate.
- Lazy-load content/media when appropriate.
- Avoid large dependencies for small features.
- Avoid unnecessary animation libraries.
- Prefer caching/revalidation when appropriate.
- Keep pages fast and lightweight.
- Do not optimize blindly; verify the actual bottleneck when possible.
